From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:53:59 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 197/297] Meridian: the agent's tab stays visible and drawn
 while it works in it

An agent's tab in the background, or in a covered or minimized window, is now
"visible" to its page for 3 minutes after the agent's last call, as a tab
being shared is (visibilityState, requestAnimationFrame, lists and dialogs
that draw only when shown); the person's active tab stays as it is.
Screenshots of a tab that isn't on the screen take one frame of a video
capture, as Chrome's tab previews. Test switch
--meridian-test-agent-awake-seconds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
